{
  "name": "WF2 Start task",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Every minute",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "minutes",
              "minutesInterval": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "List open issues",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/AdamHoppe98/Factory/issues?state=open&per_page=100",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "githubApi",
        "options": {}
      },
      "credentials": {
        "githubApi": {
          "id": "CcLRRNf9ryjsAy1J",
          "name": "Github Factory"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Pick approved issue",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One task is built at a time: if any issue is Building, start nothing.\n// Otherwise pick Adam's oldest Approved issue.\nconst has = (issue, name) => issue.labels.some(l => l.name === name);\n\nconst issues = $input.all().map(i => i.json).filter(i => i.number && !i.pull_request);\nif (issues.some(i => has(i, 'Building'))) return [];\n\nconst next = issues\n  .filter(i => i.user?.login === 'AdamHoppe98' && has(i, 'Approved'))\n  .sort((a, b) => a.number - b.number)[0];\nif (!next) return [];\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  number: next.number,\n  title: next.title,\n} }];"
      },
      "notes": "Why Code: the rule needs all issues at once (nothing Building, then the oldest Approved). One short node instead of Filter + Aggregate + IF + Sort + Limit."
    },
    {
      "id": "a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011",
      "name": "Remove Approved",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        660,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "url": "=https://api.github.com/repos/AdamHoppe98/Factory/issues/{{ $('Pick approved issue').first().json.number }}/labels/Approved",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "githubApi",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "fullResponse": true,
              "neverError": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "githubApi": {
          "id": "CcLRRNf9ryjsAy1J",
          "name": "Github Factory"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Label first, comment second: the next poll sees Building and starts nothing else. 404 = Adam removed Approved meanwhile."
    },
    {
      "id": "a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012",
      "name": "Still Approved?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        880,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.statusCode === 200 && !$json.body.some(l => ['Ideas', 'Refining', 'Ready for approval', 'Approved', 'Building', 'Waiting for you', 'Stuck', 'Your QA', 'Done'].includes(l.name)) }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "notes": "200 = the old state label was there. If Adam set another state meanwhile, his label wins."
    },
    {
      "id": "a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013",
      "name": "Add Building",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1100,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "=https://api.github.com/repos/AdamHoppe98/Factory/issues/{{ $('Pick approved issue').first().json.number }}/labels",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "githubApi",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ labels: ['Building'] }) }}",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "fullResponse": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "credentials": {
        "githubApi": {
          "id": "CcLRRNf9ryjsAy1J",
          "name": "Github Factory"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Post run command",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.github",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        1320,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "issue",
        "operation": "createComment",
        "owner": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "AdamHoppe98"
        },
        "repository": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "Factory"
        },
        "issueNumber": "={{ $('Pick approved issue').first().json.number }}",
        "body": "=<!-- factory:status -->\n**Building.** Start the agent by hand on the Mac, from the Factory repo:\n\n```\nscripts/run-manual.sh {{ $('Pick approved issue').first().json.number }}\n```\n\nIt works on branch `issue-{{ $('Pick approved issue').first().json.number }}` with the latest spec. When the agent is done, push the branch and open a PR with `Closes #{{ $('Pick approved issue').first().json.number }}`. WF3 then moves this issue to `Your QA`.\n\nIf the agent has a question, answer it here and set `Approved` again. If it gets stuck, set `Stuck`."
      },
      "credentials": {
        "githubApi": {
          "id": "CcLRRNf9ryjsAy1J",
          "name": "Github Factory"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Basic A: Adam runs the agent. Basic B (T2.4) replaces this with POST /runs."
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Every minute": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "List open issues",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "List open issues": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Pick approved issue",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Pick approved issue": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Remove Approved",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Remove Approved": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Still Approved?",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Still Approved?": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Add Building",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ],
        []
      ]
    },
    "Add Building": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Post run command",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  }
}
